{"description":"Toronto's tech scene moves fast. But the stories that really matter - the pivots, the hard calls, the lessons learned the hard way - rarely get told.\nAt our monthly Together Toronto series, we bring founders onto the stage to share what it looks like to build a company here. Honest behind-the-scenes conversations from entrepreneurs who've taken bold bets, hit unexpected walls, and figured out how to keep moving.\n\nWhat to expect:\n🎤  Founder stories with the specifics left in \n🤝 A room of builders, operators, and investors \n💡 Conversations that challenge how you think about your own company\nWhether you're launching your first thing, scaling a team, or just curious about how Toronto's best companies get built - there's a seat here for you.\nWho you'll hear from:\n🎙️ Ankita Sharma, CEO, Philer: Left a law firm to automate home closings, now approved by the Law Society of Ontario\n\n🎙️ Raghav Midha, Co-Founder & CEO, Terminal: YC S23, building the Plaid of trucking data, Series A led by Battery Ventures\n\n🎙️ Lylia Djait-Paulien, Co-Founder & CEO, Tyce: Spent a decade drafting proposals in corporate, now building AI for engineering and construction documents\n\n🎙️ Mike Masterson, Managing Partner, Supermoon Capital, Co-founded Nevro, which went public in 2014, now backs early-stage founders\n\nThis isn't just an event. It's your community.\nCome ready to listen, connect, and meet the people building what's next.\n\nAdd-On: YC W27 Application Info Session\n5:00-6:00PM, before doors open\n\nYC applications for the Winter 2027 batch close November 2.\nOne hour with YC alumni.\nWhat to expect:\n🎯 Live application reviews, in the room \n🧠 What YC actually screens for, from people who got in \n📈 How to tighten your idea, traction, and founder story \n🤝 A tight-knit room of builders on the same path\nWalk in with your application. Walk out sharper.\nSpots are limited. Approval required. Select the YC (W27) Applicant Pass above and our team will be in touch.\n\nAgenda\n5:00–6:00 PM | Y Combinator Application Info Session (By application only)\n6:00–7:00PM | Doors open and networking\n7:00–8:30PM | Community open mic, speakers presentations and fireside chat\n8:30-9:00PM | Resume networking\n9:00PM | End of event and After Party (Offsite)\n\n\nCo-organized with the Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus Ecosystem team, connecting innovators and leaders shaping the future of tech.\n\nTechTO is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Y Combinator. Many TechTO members, speakers, and sponsors are alumni of the YC program, including TechTO’s co-founder.\nAll tickets are non-transferable and non-refundable. By attending, you acknowledge and consent to photography and video recording, and agree to subscribe to our newsletter.","organizer":"TechTO"}